# Line endings are part of the reproducibility claim here, not a style question.
#
# `python -m recon.generate` must reproduce the committed dataset byte for byte
# on any machine. That only holds if git hands the checkout back exactly as the
# generator writes it, so each kind of file is pinned to what its writer emits.

# Everything text is LF in the repository and in the working tree.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The three source CSVs are written by csv.writer, whose lineterminator is CRLF
# on every platform. Git must not normalise them, or a Linux checkout would
# differ from what the generator writes by one byte per line.
*.csv -text

# The answer key is written with newline="\n" explicitly, for the same reason
# from the other direction.
ground_truth.json text eol=lf

# Binary.
*.woff2 binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
